From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:41:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virgl: keep the blob identity of a handle imported twice

The DRM winsys keeps one virgl_hw_res per GEM handle and hands it out
again for a later import of the same handle, but that path returned
before reporting the resource's blob_mem. The second virgl_resource thus
looked like a classic resource: the winsys stride and offset were
discarded as guest-storage information a classic resource does not have,
and the staging decision the first import made for a blob was never made
for it, so a map of the texture went for the non-mappable blob again and
failed.

Android's window buffers are the case. A window surface imports a buffer
every time it dequeues it, and an earlier import of the same buffer is
still alive when its age says the contents are wanted. eglSwapBuffers
worked, but every frame after a buffer's first read back
GL_OUT_OF_MEMORY from glReadPixels, and the dEQP-EGL buffer_age,
preserve_swap, color_clears and render families failed.

Report res->blob_mem on the cached path as well.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gallium/winsys/virgl/drm/virgl_drm_winsys.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/drm/virgl_drm_winsys.c b/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/drm/virgl_drm_winsys.c
index 9258a4da0ac029a50baed828287a7d769789fef8..aa5b7749ed16900a79c5325be1bc755a8944ee8a 100644
--- a/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/drm/virgl_drm_winsys.c
+++ b/src/gallium/winsys/virgl/drm/virgl_drm_winsys.c
@@ -543,6 +543,10 @@ virgl_drm_winsys_resource_create_handle(struct virgl_winsys *qws,
       if (ref == 1)
          res->needed_references++;
 
+      /* A second import of a handle is the same resource as the first, so it
+       * is the same kind of resource.
+       */
+      *blob_mem = res->blob_mem;
       goto done;
    }
 
